    "id": "product-architecture",
    "family": "layering",
    "binding": "authored",
    "question": "Which layer holds which station of the traceability spine?",
    "idea": "The spine runs from a capability through a work item and an ADR or spec to the ledger, four of the six layers hold its stations, and the pull request it crosses is held by none.",
    "title": "The six knowledge layers along the traceability spine",
    "kicker": "The knowledge model",
    "description": "The axis is the five stations of the traceability spine: capability, work item, ADR or spec, pull request, ledger. WHAT holds capability, WORK holds the work item and also reaches ADR or spec because specs live in project-management, HOW holds ADR or spec, and TRACE holds the ledger. The spine enters each of those four layers at a disc and runs left to right in the source's order; it crosses the pull request station between HOW and TRACE, where no layer holds it. WHY and RULES hold no station and draw no bar. Beside its name, WHY is marked human-owned and WHAT is marked as updated every ship.",
    "caption": "The spine runs through WHAT, WORK, HOW and TRACE in that order, and the pull request it crosses on the way to the ledger is held by no layer.",
